a secret deal reportedly allowed some of  the most notorious Isis fighters to  escape from a besieged Syrian city with  their weapons our partners at the BBC  say 250 fighters were permitted to leave  Raqqa they got out with 3,500 family  members to Isis controlled territory now  the report says their convoy included  nearly 50 rented trucks 13 buses and  more than 100 Isis vehicles 10 trucks  were loaded with weapons the BBC says  the US and British led coalition knew  about the deal brokered by Syrian  diplomatic forces democratic forces  rather and they actually monitored the  Exodus  here's an excerpt of Quinten  Somerville's report the world was told  only a few dozen local fighters were  being let go nor foreigners and no  weapons but the trucks were crammed full  of Fighters some wearing suicide belts  all were heavily armed after days of  searching we picked up the trail  at a truck stop on the outskirts of  tadka here we discovered the drivers all  civilians who drove is to freedom  they've been hired by the Kurdish led  Syrian democratic forces it was the  longest journey of their lives their  trucks were rigged with is bombs in case  the deal collapsed they've been told  they were picking up only a few hundred  civilians that it would be a quick job  they ended up driving day and night for  three days this couldn't look like the  Islamic states escape to victory  so the SDF insisted there will be no  Flags and no banners instead is vital  sat boldly on top of the trucks the axle  on one lorry broke it was so overloaded  with is weaponry Pentagon spokesman says  the United States was not part of this  deal but the spokesman also points out  the u.s. was not prepared to bomb buses  full of women and children
 

